## Incident 4 (P2): entity resolution is inert on pure-PDF corpora, silently

`muck index` on this 596-doc corpus reported `entities: 4, mentions: 8`. Per
`src/muck/extract/entities.py:3-4`, mentions come only from (a) a gazetteer built from JSON
`entity_fields` and (b) bill-number regex. A parse-only corpus has neither, so
`--person/--org` filtering and the entity network are dead weight — with no warning.
Also: `pyproject.toml:23` declares a `spacy` extra that is never imported anywhere.

**Suggested fixes:**
1. Minimum: when `index` finishes with ~0 entities on a corpus with parsed docs, emit a
   `notice` in the JSON explaining why and what still works (search/grep/aggregate/cluster).
2. Better: wire the declared-but-unused spacy extra into an optional NER mention extractor
   for parsed text, feeding the existing resolver. (Or delete the extra — it currently
   promises capability that doesn't exist.)

