- SQL: `WHERE regexp(?, c.text) ... LIMIT ?`. **No `ORDER BY`** — ordering is whatever SQLite yields (effectively `chunks` rowid / insertion order), truncated at `k`. There is no relevance ranking for grep.
- Per-row `re.search(pattern, r["text"], re.IGNORECASE)` (line 97) recomputes the match to feed `_snippet` a match-centered window. The `m.group(0)` (first match text) is the `around` arg. **Only the first match** is windowed; offsets of the match are not returned to the caller (only `chunk_id` + snippet string). Note the regexp UDF and this per-row search both hardcode `re.IGNORECASE`.
- Returns list of `(chunk_id, snippet)` tuples (2-tuples, unlike BM25's 3-tuples).

